---
id: org.dxos.plugin.codeGraph
name: CodeGraphPlugin
version: 0.1.0
---

A canvas of the codebase, built from code-index. Boxes are resources in the index (packages, files,
symbols); arrows are facts between them (imports, package dependencies). The assistant fills and reshapes
a graph by querying the index. The canvas lays the same graph out with the illustrator's semantic engine,
a force-directed layout, or by dependency rank, and can show the illustrator's full drawing.

Dev only: the page reaches the index through a `vite dev` route that runs `code-index mcp` beside the app
(`tauri dev` loads the same dev server). See `docs/DESIGN.md`.

## Extensions

The following extension dialects are used in this document.
Each extension is defined in the Appendix or resolved via its URI.

| Term        | URI                            |
|-------------|--------------------------------|
| `type`      | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`       |
| `feat`      | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`       |
| `scenario`  | `org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0`   |
| `component` | `org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0`  |
| `op`        | `org.dxos.mdl.op@1.1`         |
| `test`      | `org.dxos.mdl.test@1.0`       |
| `step`      | `org.dxos.mdl.step@1.0`       |
| `decision`  | `org.dxos.mdl.decision@1.0`   |

## Types

```mdl
type CodeGraph
  desc: A curated view of the code index. Boxes and arrows are held inline; each box stands for a resource in the index.
  fields:
    name?: string
    layout?: Layout
    grouped?: boolean        # frame boxes by package (illustrator layout and drawing)
    nodes: Node[]
    edges: Edge[]
```

```mdl
type Node
  desc: One box.
  fields:
    id: string             # the resource IRI, e.g. https://dxos.org/deus/package/@dxos/echo
    label: string
    kind: NodeKind
    group?: string         # the package directory; the illustrator frames boxes by it
    position?: Position    # where the user dragged the box
```

```mdl
type Edge
  desc: One arrow, from the subject to the object of a triple.
  fields:
    from: string
    to: string
    kind?: string          # the predicate's local name, e.g. imports, usesPackage
```

```mdl
type NodeKind
  literals: package | file | symbol | module | spec | other
```

```mdl
type Layout
  literals: illustrator | force | rank | diagram
```

## Operations

```mdl
op query
  key: org.dxos.operation.codeGraph.query
  desc: Runs a SPARQL SELECT over the index and returns the rows; draws nothing.
```

```mdl
op inspect
  key: org.dxos.operation.codeGraph.inspect
  desc: Returns one resource's outgoing facts and incoming counts.
```

```mdl
op read
  key: org.dxos.operation.codeGraph.read
  desc: Returns a graph's boxes, arrows and layout.
```

```mdl
op addFromQuery
  key: org.dxos.operation.codeGraph.addFromQuery
  desc: Runs a SELECT and draws its rows; ?from/?to rows are arrows, ?node rows are boxes.
```

```mdl
op addNodes
  key: org.dxos.operation.codeGraph.addNodes
  desc: Adds boxes for resources and connects every box pair the index links by imports or usesPackage.
```

```mdl
op addNeighbors
  key: org.dxos.operation.codeGraph.addNeighbors
  desc: Adds the neighbours of boxes along one predicate, outward, inward or both.
```

```mdl
op remove
  key: org.dxos.operation.codeGraph.remove
  desc: Removes boxes and their arrows, or everything.
```

```mdl
op setLayout
  key: org.dxos.operation.codeGraph.setLayout
  desc: Chooses the layout, optionally forgets dragged positions, and optionally turns grouping by package on or off.
```

```mdl
op runCommand
  key: org.dxos.operation.codeGraph.runCommand
  desc: Carries out one short command with its own fast model, which may only add SPARQL results or remove boxes by a text filter; a decision model ends the loop.
```

## Components

```mdl
component CodeGraphArticle
  desc: The article surface. A toolbar picks the layout, groups by package and resets positions; the body is the canvas or the drawing, with a details panel for the selected box and the same panel as a card on hover.
  props:
    subject: CodeGraph
```

```mdl
component CodeGraphCanvas
  desc: react-ui-canvas-editor's Graph2DView with one box per resource, as plugin-projects' FeatureCanvas uses it: the graph as a dynamic 2D layout in the shared scene editor. Arrangement and the placed positions (pinned shapes) place the boxes. A box shows a symbol's own name and a coloured tag of its kind from the index. Package frames are the canvas's own diagram shapes, on a backdrop layer under the boxes and arrows.
```

```mdl
component CodeGraphDiagram
  desc: plugin-illustrator's SceneSvg drawing of the semantic layout, read-only, with package frames and routed arrows.
```

```mdl
component NodeDetails
  desc: The selected resource's facts, with expand and remove actions.
```

```mdl
component CommandBar
  desc: A floating button (or `/`) that opens a one-line command field over the canvas, with a microphone toggle for spoken commands and a line for the outcome and the trailer.
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Read the index from the app
  req F-1.1: A same-origin dev-server route answers read-only code-index tools by running `code-index mcp` as a child process.
  req F-1.2: The route accepts only loopback callers and JSON requests, so other pages and machines cannot read the source tree.
  req F-1.3: Without the route (a deployed build), every operation fails with an error that names the missing route.
```

```mdl
feat F-2: The assistant shapes the graph
  req F-2.1: The Code Graph skill offers query, inspect, read, addFromQuery, addNodes, addNeighbors, remove and setLayout, and the space's addObject to create a graph.
  req F-2.2: A chat about a CodeGraph object carries the skill (SkillsAnnotation).
  req F-2.3: Adding never duplicates a box or an arrow, and a box an arrow needs is added with it.
  req F-2.4: An addition that would take a graph past 300 boxes fails whole with `LimitError`.
```

```mdl
feat F-3: Two layouts on one canvas
  req F-3.1: The illustrator layout solves the graph as semantic DSL and places canvas boxes at the solved centres; when the graph is grouped it frames each package's boxes, the package box included, in a tinted frame titled with the package's name, one colour per package.
  req F-3.2: The force layout uses the canvas's own force arrangement; rank uses its fewest-crossings arrangement.
  req F-3.3: Dragging a box saves only its position; boxes the user did not move stay under the layout.
  req F-3.4: The diagram layout renders the illustrator's full drawing with SceneSvg.
```

```mdl
feat F-4: Inspect a box
  req F-4.1: Double-clicking a box opens its facts from the index.
  req F-4.2: The details panel expands the box's dependencies or dependents, or removes it.
```

feat F-5: Single commands
  req F-5.1: A command bar, apart from the chat assistant, takes one typed or spoken command and runs it with RunCommand.
  req F-5.2: The command model sees the graph as it is and may only add the rows of a SPARQL SELECT or remove boxes matching a text filter (`*`, `kind:<kind>`, `/regex/`, or text).
  req F-5.3: Between turns a decision model (the space's default, Clef on Workers AI unless configured) judges whether the command is done; a failed or empty action earns another turn without asking, and a turn that only removed boxes ends the command; at most 3 turns.
  req F-5.4: A command adds at most 40 boxes; the rest are left out and summarised in a trailer (counts by kind and package, and a few names) shown to the user and the model.
  req F-5.5: Speaking uses Whistle on the device: with the microphone on, each pause ends a command.
  req F-5.6: Before the first model call, the packages and exported symbols the command names are looked up in the index and given to the model as exact IRIs; the lookup is skipped after 1.5 s.
  req F-5.7: A verbose toggle in the bar, remembered per browser, lists every step of the last command (lookup, model call, add, remove, judge) with its time, its token counts or row counts, and the SPARQL or filter it ran.

## Acceptance

```mdl
scenario T-1: Draw package dependencies
  given: an index of this repository, and composer-app under `vite dev`
  when: the assistant is asked to draw the @dxos packages plugin-markdown depends on
  then: a code graph shows plugin-markdown with an arrow to each dependency, laid out by the illustrator
```

```mdl
scenario T-2: Switch layout
  given: a code graph with boxes
  when: the user picks the force layout
  then: the same boxes are re-placed by the force arrangement, and the graph's layout field reads force
```

scenario T-3: Clear the graph
  given: a code graph with boxes
  when: the user runs the command "clear the graph"
  then: the graph is empty after one model turn

scenario T-4: Show a package's exports
  given: a code graph showing unrelated packages
  when: the user runs "show me the ECHO package exports"
  then: the graph shows only the exports of @dxos/echo

scenario T-5: Draw dependents
  given: an empty code graph
  when: the user runs "What depends on identity service in halo"
  then: the graph shows the identity service with an arrow from each file that imports it, the first 40 boxes at most and a trailer for the rest

## QA

```mdl
test QA-1: Draw and reshape a package graph
  desc: The primary journey — create a graph, fill it from the index, expand a box, switch layouts.
  actors: human, agent
  covers: [F-1.1, F-2.1, F-2.3, F-3.1, F-3.2, F-5.1]
  status: passing           # 2026-10-23; driven by a Playwright script against `vite dev`: steps 1-3 by `invoke`, step 4 and the details panel's Expand by clicks. The assistant chat itself was not exercised (no model key in the sandbox).
  given:
    - the index is built (`bun tools/code-index/bin/code-index.ts index`) and no other code-index process holds it
    - composer-app runs under `moon run composer-app:serve`
    - space: a space is open
    - plugin-code-graph is enabled
  steps:
    - name: Create the graph
      do: In the navtree, click + and choose Code Graph. Name it "QA Code Graph".
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.addObject { object: { "@type": "org.dxos.type.codeGraph", name: "QA Code Graph", nodes: [], edges: [] } }
      capture: graph
      expect: an empty Code Graph article opens with the message asking the assistant to draw here
    - name: Draw a package's dependencies
      do: Ask the assistant to draw the @dxos packages that @dxos/plugin-markdown depends on.
      invoke: [op:addFromQuery] { graph: $graph.object, sparql: "SELECT ?from ?to WHERE { BIND(<https://dxos.org/deus/package/@dxos/plugin-markdown> AS ?from) ?from deus:usesPackage ?to . ?to deus:name ?name . FILTER(STRSTARTS(?name, \"@dxos/\")) }" }
      expect: boxes for plugin-markdown and its @dxos dependencies, with arrows from plugin-markdown, placed on a grid
      assert: return $result.addedEdges > 0 && $result.nodes === $result.addedNodes;
    - name: Expand a dependency
      do: Double-click the @dxos/echo box and choose Expand dependencies.
      invoke: [op:addNeighbors] { graph: $graph.object, nodes: ["pkg:@dxos/echo"] }
      expect: the packages echo depends on appear, with arrows from echo
      assert: return $result.addedNodes > 0;
    - name: Switch to the force layout
      do: Click the force-directed layout button in the toolbar.
      invoke: [op:setLayout] { graph: $graph.object, layout: "force" }
      expect: the same boxes are re-placed; none overlap
    - name: Run a command
      do: Press /, type "clear the graph" and press Enter.
      invoke: [op:runCommand] { graph: $graph.object, command: "clear the graph" }
      expect: the canvas empties and the command bar says what it did
      assert: return $result.removedNodes > 0;
  after:
    - name: Delete the graph
      do: Right-click "QA Code Graph" in the navtree and choose Delete.
      expect: the graph leaves the navtree
```

```mdl
test QA-2: Single commands
  desc: The command bar, apart from the chat: replace the graph with a package's exports, draw what depends on a service, then clear it.
  actors: human, agent
  covers: [F-5.1, F-5.2, F-5.3, F-5.4]
  status: passing           # 2026-10-23; driven by autocue/commands.mjs against `vite dev` with EDGE preview; 9.3 s for the first command (index process cold), 4–5 s after. Speech was not exercised (no microphone in the sandbox).
  given:
    - the index is built (`bun tools/code-index/bin/code-index.ts index`) and no other code-index process holds it
    - composer-app runs under `moon run composer-app:serve` with an AI service (EDGE preview, `DX_EDGE_BASE_URL=https://preview.dxos.network/`)
    - space: a space is open
    - plugin-code-graph is enabled
    - a Code Graph named "Commands" is open
  steps:
    - name: Show a package's exports
      do: Press /, type "show me the ECHO package exports" and press Enter.
      expect: the graph shows @dxos/echo with an arrow to each module it exports, and the bar says what it drew
    - name: Draw what depends on a service
      do: Type "What depends on identity service in halo" and press Enter.
      expect: the echo exports are replaced by Identity.Service and the symbols and operations that use it
    - name: Clear the graph
      do: Type "clear the graph" and press Enter.
      expect: the canvas is empty
```

## Changelog

Every change to this spec adds a decision, newest last. See `lang/changelog.mdl` for the attribution rules.

```mdl
decision D-1: A Composer plugin integrates with code-index; it may work only under `vite dev` or in Tauri.
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1]
```

```mdl
decision D-2: The plugin's article is a canvas of the code graph, and the assistant gets tools to query and change that graph.
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [CodeGraphArticle, F-2]
```

```mdl
decision D-3: The canvas lays the graph out both with the illustrator's layout and as a force-directed graph, sharing the canvas and illustrator code the way feature maps do.
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [CodeGraphCanvas, F-3]
```

```mdl
decision D-4: The page reaches code-index through a dev-server route that runs `code-index mcp` as a child process. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1.1, F-1.2]
  why: The index's store is single-process behind a native addon, and the code-index web server has no SPARQL route; the MCP server already serves the read-only tools.
  rejected: Opening the store in the vite process, which would hold its lock and load the addon there.
```

```mdl
decision D-5: One canvas serves the illustrator, force and rank layouts; the illustrator's semantic engine supplies box positions as the canvas overlay, and a fourth view shows the illustrator's own drawing. Fills in [D-3].
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [CodeGraphCanvas, CodeGraphDiagram, F-3.1, F-3.2, F-3.4]
  why: Feature maps use react-ui-canvas's dynamic projection, which already has a force arrangement; feeding it illustrator positions compares both layouts on one component.
```

```mdl
decision D-6: Illustrator positions are centred on the origin, and the canvas refits when they arrive. Fills in [D-5].
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [CodeGraphCanvas, F-3.1]
  why: The engine's coordinates start at its own origin and arrive after the canvas's first fit, so the graph opened off-centre and too small to read.
```

```mdl
decision D-7: The skill creates a graph with the space's addObject from a typed draft; the plugin has no create operation. Fills in [D-2].
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-2.1]
  why: An assistant cannot pass a live object back from a tool call, so it needs a draft form, which addObject already accepts; a create operation that also saved the object duplicated it.
  rejected: A create operation that adds the graph to the space itself.
```

```mdl
decision D-8: A graph holds at most 300 boxes; an addition past that fails whole with LimitError. Fills in [D-2].
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-2.4]
  why: An assistant expanding without end would grow the document and the layouts past what stays fast or readable.
  rejected: Truncating the addition silently.
```

```mdl
decision D-9: Grouping by package is a saved switch on the graph, and the canvas draws the frames with its own diagram nodes on a backdrop layer. Fills in [D-5].
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-3.1]
  why: Implicit framing for 2 to 6 packages left no way to see a graph by package, or to turn frames off; the canvas already draws the illustrator's tinted group frames, and a layer under the arrows keeps them from covering the arrows.
  rejected: A frame view of the plugin's own; framing only when there are few packages.
```

```mdl
decision D-10: A single-command mode, apart from Composer's agent, runs typed or spoken commands with a model that sees the graph and may only add SPARQL results or remove boxes by a text filter; a decision model judges between turns whether to stop, and an addition past N boxes adds the first N with a trailer summarising the rest.
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [CommandBar, F-5]
```

```mdl
decision D-11: The command loop asks for one structured step per turn (actions and a sentence) from Claude Haiku rather than running a tool-calling agent; the judge is the AI service's default decision model. Fills in [D-10].
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-5.2, F-5.3]
  why: A command should take one model round trip; several actions fit in one step, and a decision model answers "is this done" faster and cheaper than another language-model turn.
  rejected: Reusing the chat assistant's tool loop, which plans and explains at length.
```

```mdl
decision D-12: A command adds at most 40 boxes; a failed or empty action earns a turn without the judge, a turn that only removed boxes ends the command without it, and with no decision model a command stops after its first successful turn. Fills in [D-10].
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-5.3, F-5.4]
  why: Forty boxes stay readable under every layout; retrying a refused query, or accepting a removal that did what it said, needs no judgement, so asking would only add latency.
```

```mdl
decision D-13: Whistle moves from plugin-transcription's stories to `@dxos/plugin-transcription/Whistle` so the command bar can use it. Fills in [D-10].
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-5.5]
  why: The command bar asked for the microphone and Whistle; the stories held the only copy of the on-device speech hook.
```

```mdl
decision D-14: The command loop looks up the packages and symbols a command names before the model's first turn, and the article loads the index's package list when it opens. Fills in [D-10].
  date: 2026-10-26
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-5.6]
  why: A model that guessed names with CONTAINS filters drew the wrong things or wrote queries the index refused, and each retry cost another 2 s model call; an exact lookup on a warm index costs about 10 ms. The first query on a cold index takes seconds, so opening the article pays for it.
  rejected: More turns or a larger model, which add seconds to every command.
```

```mdl
decision D-15: RunCommand returns a trace of timed steps, and the command bar shows it in a verbose mode the user turns on. Fills in [D-10].
  date: 2026-10-26
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-5.7, CommandBar]
  why: A slow or wrong command could not be explained from the outcome line; the trace shows where the time went and which query the model ran.
```

```mdl
decision D-16: The judge is the space's default decision model, which is Cloudflare's Clef unless configured, and Code Graph depends on the TypeSafe plugin so that a decision model is always there. Fills in [D-11].
  date: 2026-10-26
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-5.3]
  why: With TypeSafe off (it defaults on only in dev builds) no resolver served decision models, so every command stopped after its first turn; Clef answers through EDGE with no key, in about 0.3 s once signed in.
```

```mdl
decision D-17: CodeGraphCanvas draws through react-ui-scene's Graph2DView, the graph as a dynamic Layout2D in the shared scene editor, in place of react-ui-canvas's dynamic projection and View store. Fills in [D-5].
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [CodeGraphCanvas]
  why: The View model and ViewStore are being retired (react-ui-canvas COMMON-CORE-PLAN E.5/E.6); a dragged box is now a pinned shape, and its centre is the position the article stores, so nothing the article persists changes.
```

```mdl
decision D-18: CodeGraphCanvas takes Graph2DView from react-ui-canvas-editor, where it moved when react-ui-scene was removed. Fills in [D-17].
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [CodeGraphCanvas]
  why: Graph2DView draws a graph in the shared scene editor, so it is an editor view, not a surface part.
```
